{"$schema":"../schemas/Causal-Decision-Model.json","meta":{"uuid":"e6e52260-c176-5d76-bbc1-e3df8e2c9e14","name":"Coffee Purchasing Decision","summary":"Static pack-in model, loaded by default. For deciding whether to purchase regular or fair trade coffee, and how much. This CDM models the impact to workers and environment, to ultimately track social/environmental and financial impacts as main outcomes. This model is a working example of a complete, runnable decision model contained in schema-compliant JSON. It has multiple scripts, used as Evaluatable Assets in a single Runnable Model with 4 elements. It has many I/O values connected to various Diagram Elements via Controls.\n\n**NOTE:** This Decision Model is intended for demonstration purposes only. It does not accurately represent the real-world impacts of a coffee purchasing decision. The algorithms for determining environmental and social impacts are largely arbitrary. Prices are inaccurate. etc.","documentation":{"content":"This CDD was authored by Dr. Lorien Pratt.\nSource: https://www.lorienpratt.com/a-framework-for-how-data-informs-decisions/\n\nAdapted for OpenDI schema compliance and in-browser simulation by Isaac Kellogg.","MIMEType":"text/plain"},"version":"0.1","draft":true},"runnableModels":[{"meta":{"uuid":"fbe76400-692f-56c7-bcbd-2737c1cb1fef","name":"Coffee: Runnable Decision Model"},"elements":[{"meta":{"name":"Get Coffee Totals","uuid":"de62d4fe-c117-47bd-9390-e88491f97353","summary":"Calculate the total prices of all coffee purchases."},"inputs":["a656a366-9dbc-55c9-ad0c-23efc66d4ece","f6219a74-f87b-5d8a-be02-abbbc753d005","312892eb-440b-55c6-93e2-f80da4c3bd8e","20a0991f-e8f2-504e-af1d-e192f7ea567d"],"outputs":["b5d1193c-9d68-5a44-a7f2-3cf49babf5d5","4ed61cf7-f5a2-5c86-a6fe-1a5418d8ab8b","88078967-f137-557a-bb47-2ddaef51240b"],"functionName":"getCoffeeTotals","evaluatableAsset":"160b0a8f-2b2a-517f-b160-2cb1a0f946fb"},{"meta":{"name":"Get Environmental Impact","uuid":"63246be1-8c71-48e2-a57e-9d9d